# the compilation of a module for a register machine, see doc/machine/emit.md
#
# this is the one entry a consumer of the library calls to turn a module the
# pass schedule has run on into mink's object in memory. every function with a
# body goes through the steps of STAGES in order: selection with the
# convention's clobbers, the constant-time check of a selected function that
# requires constant time, allocation over the locations the machine allows, the
# frame, the lowering of copies to the set's moves, the establishing of the
# configuration states instructions run under, the expansion of loops into
# their steps and layout. the laid out functions are handed to masc in one
# object. the sequence is stated once, here, so a step is added in one place.
# the target reaches its selection table, frame code and moves through the
# record of its set in the registry the family hands in, so this names no set
# and imports no registry. a checked compilation verifies every function after
# every step, and the machine form text and masc's listing are written when
# asked. a function that names extensions past the build's is made under the
# build's selection widened by them, whose context, moves and frame code the
# session opens once for each distinct set.

